          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em
              Dependent linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            should be some kind of combination of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
            %em homotopy
            type theory (
            %a{:href => "#Schreiber14"}> Schreiber 2014
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Riley22"} Riley 2022
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p One of the most important is a theory that includes both “linear types” and “nonlinear types”, where the linear types may be dependent on the nonlinear types. The nonlinear types might also be allowed to depend on each other, but in this theory the linear types are not allowed to depend on each other.
          %p There are other approaches to dependent linear type theory that do allow some sort of dependence between linear types, but we will not (yet) discuss them on this page.
          %h2#syntax Syntax
          %p
            Details are still somewhat in the making: An extension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LF"} LF
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            by dependent linear types appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Pfenning96"}> Pfenning 96
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#WCFW03"} WCFW 03
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/system+L"} system L
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Spiwack14"}> Spiwack 14, section 5
            ).
          %p
            Proposals for an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            for dependent linear type theory appear in (
            %a{:href => "#Vakar14"}> Vákár 14
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KPB15"} KPB 15
          %h2#semantics Semantics
          %p
            One sort of dependent linear type theory should have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} indexed monoidal (∞,1)-categories
            – see there for detailed discussion.
          %h3#nonhomotopy_version Non-homotopy version
          %p
            Notice that the following relation between syntax and semantics are well established (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
            for details):
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantics
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} multiplicative intuitionistic linear type theory
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+categories"} locally cartesian closed categories
          %p
            Here the correspondence in the first line works by interpreting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X]
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\otimes}
            and by interpreting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunctions"} conjunctions
            (as far as they exist) as follows:
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+conjunction"} multiplicative conjunction
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊸
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \multimap
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+implication"} linear implication
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\bot
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+negation"} linear negation
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
          %p
            The correspondence in the second line works by forming for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            its system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma] \mapsto \mathcal{C}_{/[\Gamma]}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo }
                  %mo ↔
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\Gamma \vdash a \colon A
                  \\right\}
                  \\leftrightarrow
                  \\left\{
                  (\ast \stackrel{[a]}{\longrightarrow} [A])
                  \\in Mor(\mathcal{C}_{/[\Gamma]})
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, the system of slice categories has good
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            in that for every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f] \colon [\Gamma_1]\to [\Gamma_2]
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi f
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi f
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{[\Gamma_1]}
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{[f]_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{[f]^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{[f]_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{[\Gamma_2]}
          %p
            satisfying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            along a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \Gamma_1 \to \Gamma_2
            of contexts, and for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            of the dependent type theory syntax, respectively:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo }
                  %mo ↔
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\underset{f^{-1}(-)}{\sum}
                  , \; f \;,
                  \\underset{f^{-1}(-)}{\prod}
                  \\right\}
                  \\leftrightarrow
                  \\left\{
                  [f]_! \dashv [f]^\ast \dashv [f]_\ast
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now since a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            is in particular a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma] \mapsto (\mathcal{C}_{/[\Gamma]})^\times
            to assignments
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Gamma] \mapsto (\mathcal{C}_{[\Gamma]})^\otimes
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            (possibly but not necessarily the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            in the above way.
          %p
            More explicitly, following the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of dependent linear type theory should have for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            a
            = succeed "/possibly-non-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}_{\Gamma}, \otimes, 1)
            and for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contexts"} contexts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; \Gamma_1 \longrightarrow \Gamma_2
            functorially an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f_! \dashv f^\ast \dashv f_\ast)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{C}_{\Gamma_1}
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{f_\ast}{\rightarrow}}}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{\Gamma_2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            and where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
            are to be thought of as linear analogs of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            should be a strong
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+functor"} closed monoidal functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
            for consecutive such adjoint triples.
          %p
            Equivalently this is an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+closed+monoidal+category"} indexed closed monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} indexed monoidal (∞,1)-category
          %p
            In
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            such a “linear hyperdoctrine” is known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"} six operations
                yoga in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+context"} Wirtmüller flavor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+theory"} geometric homotopy theory
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
            on
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                dependent linear
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p
            Details (of what?) are written out in (
            %a{:href => "#Vakar14"}> Vakar 14
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              is a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
              means that it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast(X\otimes Y)\simeq (f^\ast X)\otimes (f^\ast Y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              If monoidal categories involved are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+categories"} closed monoidal categories
              then the condition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
              is equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              also being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+closed+functor"} strong closed functor
              in that it preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast [X,Y] \simeq [f^\ast X, f^\ast Y]
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_notation Definition (Notation)
            %p
              In view of the perspective of semantics for type theory, we may omit the notational distinction between contexts and the objects that interpret them, and between dependent sum/product and the functors that interpret them. We will write the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi f
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi f
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo !
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{f}{\sum}
                    \\dashv
                    f^\ast
                    \\dashv
                    \\underset{f}{\prod}
                    \\right)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Mod(\Gamma_1)
                    \\stackrel{\stackrel{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    Mod(\Gamma_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The statement of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
              then equivalently reads like this:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi Y
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi f
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{f}{\sum}
                    \\left(
                    X \otimes f^\ast Y
                    \\right)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{f}{\sum} X
                    \\right)
                    \\otimes
                    Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
              a morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon_f
                    \\colon
                    \\underset{f}{\sum}f^\ast (-)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    (-)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction counit
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi f
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\sum_f \dashv f^\ast)
            %p
              Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{f}{\sum}
              has the interpretation of summing over all the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              of the morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              vary. Therefore it is sometime suggestive to use the notation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{f^{-1}(-)}{\sum}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{f}{\sum}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In this vein, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              any object and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_X \colon X \to \ast
              the canonical morphism to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{X}{\sum}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{p_X}{\sum}
                    \\,.
          %h3#LinearHomotopyTypeTheory Homotopy version
          %p
            This discussion of dependent linear type theory
            %a{:href => "#DependentLinearTypeTheory"} above
            has an evident straightforward refinement to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
            for details):
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantics
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-categories
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalent
                  weak
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
          %p
            This works very much along the lines of the above relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+categories"} locally cartesian closed categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            to be equipped with a suitable structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
            of morphisms. The key point is that where in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \vdash Id_X \colon Type)
            of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has semantics given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{[X]} \in \mathcal{C}_{/{[X]}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            it has semantics in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \Delta_{[X]} \in \mathcal{C}_{/X}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            “inside” the type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since the Grothendieck construction of the standard indexed monoidal
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} tangent (∞,1)-toposes
              %em linear
              types might be higher
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} jet (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            What should be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of one kind of dependent linear type theory was discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman08"}> Shulman 08
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#PontoShulman12"} Ponto-Shulman 12
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman12"} Shulman 12
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber14"} Schreiber 14
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"}> dependent type theory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+set"} quantum set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+modality"} classical modality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"}> categorical semantics
                \:
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"}> indexed monoidal (∞,1)-categories
                ,
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} tangent (∞,1)-toposes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic"}> quantum logic
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming"} quantum programming
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+quantum+system"} parameterized quantum system
          %h2#References References
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            extending
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LF"} LF
            with linear dependent types was first published in
          %ul
            %li#Pfenning96
              Iliano Cervesato,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pfenning"} Frank Pfenning
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Linear Logical Framework
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.21.1152"} web
          %p
            Note that this framework was restricted to the
            %em negative
            fragment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+linear+logic"} intuitionistic linear logic
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            (i.e.,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊸
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \multimap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi &amp;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \&amp;
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LF"} LF
            to positive connectives (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo !
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes,1,!,\exists
            ) while retaining a reasonable notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+form"} canonical form
            was later addressed by
          %ul
            %li#WCFW03
              Kevin Watkins, Iliano Cervesato,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pfenning"} Frank Pfenning
              = succeed "," do
                %em A concurrent logical framework I: Judgments and properties
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~fp/papers/CMU-CS-02-101.pdf"} web
          %p
            A dependent linear version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/system+L"} system L
            is considered in
          %ul
            %li#Spiwack14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Spiwack"}> Arnaud Spiwack
              , section 5 of:
              %em A dissection of L
              (2014) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://assert-false.science/arnaud/papers/A%20dissection%20of%20L.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p More recent work in the type-theoretic literature includes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ugo+Dal+Lago"}> Ugo Dal Lago
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear Dependent Types in a Subrecursive Setting
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~drg/bll.html"} Bounded Linear Logic Workshop
                Fontainebleau, 2013,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~drg/bll/dallago.pdf"} slides
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ugo+Dal+Lago"}> Ugo Dal Lago
                , M. Gaboardi,
                = succeed "Logical" do
                  %em Linear Dependent Types and Relative Completeness-, in
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ugo+Dal+Lago"} Ugo Dal Lago
                and B. Petit,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear dependent types in a call-by-value scenario
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Science of Computer Programming 84
            %li
              %p
                F.N. Forsberg,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Restricted linear dependent types for resource allocation
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~drg/bll.html"} Bounded Linear Logic Workshop
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~drg/bll/fredrik.pdf"} slides
            %li
              %p
                M. Gaboardi et al.,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear Dependent Types for Differential Privacy
          %p
            Proposals for a genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            for dependent linear type theory:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "SchöppStark04"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Sch%C3%B6pp"}> Ulrich Schöpp
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Stark"} Ian Stark
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Dependent Type Theory with Names and Binding
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computer Science Logic. CSL 2004
                %strong 3210
                (2004) 235–249 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-30124-0_20"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-540-30124-0_20
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://homepages.inf.ed.ac.uk/stark/names+binding.html"} web
            %li#Vakar14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthijs+V%C3%A1k%C3%A1r"}> Matthijs Vákár
                ,
                %em Syntax and Semantics of Linear Dependent Types
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0033"}> arXiv:1405.0033
                )
            %li#VakarSlides14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthijs+V%C3%A1k%C3%A1r"}> Matthijs Vákár
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Splitting the Atom of Dependent Types… or Linear and Operational Dependent Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/VakarLinearAndOperationalDTT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Vakar15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthijs+V%C3%A1k%C3%A1r"}> Matthijs Vákár
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Categorical Semantics for Linear Logical Frameworks
                %em Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures
                FoSSaCS 2015. Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol 9034. Springer 2015 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.05016"}> arXiv:1501.05016
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-46678-0_7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-46678-0_7
            %li#Vakar17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthijs+V%C3%A1k%C3%A1r"}> Matthijs Vákár
                , Section 3 of:
                %em In Search of Effectful Dependent Types
                (
